      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "We're Not Married! (1952) represents a fascinating slice of early 1950s Hollywood comedy, featuring an all-star ensemble cast including Ginger Rogers and Marilyn Monroe. The film's premise - five couples discovering their marriages aren't legally valid - brilliantly captured post-war American anxiety about domestic institutions. It shares DNA with other marriage-focused comedies of the era like The Marrying Kind (1952) and <a href=\"/movie/33575\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"33575\">Pat and Mike</a> (1952), but takes a more subversive approach by questioning the very foundation of matrimony itself."
      },
