      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film sits at a crucial junction in Hollywood's portrayal of marriage. While pre-war films often treated marriage as the happy ending, post-war cinema began examining it more critically, as in <a href=\"/movie/887\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"887\">The Best Years of Our Lives</a> (1946). We're Not Married! uses its high-concept premise to probe deeper questions about what makes a marriage real - legal documents or emotional commitment? This theme would later be explored dramatically in films like <a href=\"/movie/10712\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"10712\">Far From Heaven</a> (2002) and <a href=\"/movie/4148\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"4148\">Revolutionary Road</a> (2008)."
      }
